AllStandard -- boolean option for determining the use of all standard or smaller standard monomials
***************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

This is an optional input for the *note groebnerStratum: groebnerStratum, and
*note groebnerFamily: groebnerFamily, functions.  It takes values $true$ and
$false$.  When assigned the value $true$, the functions are computed with
respect to all standard monomials for the specified generators.  When assigned
the value $false$, the functions are computed with respect to smaller monomials
of the same degree as the specified generators but which do not lie in the
ideal.

See also
========

  * *note groebnerStratum: groebnerStratum, -- compute the ideal where a given
    is a Groebner basis
  * *note groebnerFamily: groebnerFamily, -- computes families of ideals with a
    specified initial ideal
  * *note smallerMonomials: smallerMonomials, -- returns the standard monomials
    smaller but of the same degree as given monomial(s)
  * *note standardMonomials: standardMonomials, -- computes standard monomials

Functions with optional argument named AllStandard:
===================================================

  * "groebnerFamily(...,AllStandard=>...)" -- see *note groebnerFamily:
    groebnerFamily, -- computes families of ideals with a specified initial
    ideal
  * "tailMonomials(...,AllStandard=>...)" -- see *note tailMonomials:
    tailMonomials, -- find tail monomials

