|i10 : F2 = groebnerFamily (M, L)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|              2                                      2              2        |
|o10 = ideal (a  + t a*c + t b*c + t a*d + t b*d + t c  + t c*d + t d , a*b + |
|                   1       2       4       5       3      6       7          |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                            2                2   2           |
|      t a*c + t b*c + t  a*d + t  b*d + t  c  + t  c*d + t  d , b  + t  a*c +|
|       8       9       11       12       10      13       14          15     |
|      -----------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                     2                2                      |
|      t  b*c + t  a*d + t  b*d + t  c  + t  c*d + t  d )                     |
|       16       18       19       17      20       21                        |
|                                                                             |
|                 ZZ                                                          |
|o10 : Ideal of -----[t , t ..t , t  , t  ..t  , t  , t  ..t  , t ..t , t ..t |
|               32003  3   6   7   10   13   14   17   20   21   1   2   4   5|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|, t ..t , t  ..t  , t  ..t  , t  ..t  ][a..d]                                |
|   8   9   11   12   15   16   18   19                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that $F$ and $F_2$ are the same family, in this case.

This function also works if the ring of $M$ is a skew-commutative ring. This
function produces a family of ideals in the exterior algebra. Similarly, *note
groebnerStratum: groebnerStratum, allows one to find the ideal in the commuting
coefficient variables of the family of ideals having $M$ as lead monomial
