linearPart -- returns linear part of a polynomial
*************************************************

  * Usage: 
        l = linearPart(f)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, f is a polynomial
  * Outputs:
      * l, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, l is the sum of
        the terms of f whose monomial is a variable

Description
===========

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[a,b,c];               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = a^2 + 3*b + 5*a*b*c + 2*a +b^2;|
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : linearPart f                       |
|                                        |
|o3 = 2a + 3b                            |
|                                        |
|o3 : R                                  |
+----------------------------------------+

If we have a polynomial ring over another polynomial ring, the command only
looks at the exponents on the new set of variables.

+--------------------------------+
|i4 : S = ZZ/32003[a,b,c][x,y,z];|
+--------------------------------+
|i5 : g = a*b*x + 3*y + a + b^2  |
|                                |
|                   2            |
|o5 = a*b*x + 3y + b  + a        |
|                                |
|o5 : S                          |
+--------------------------------+
|i6 : linearPart g               |
|                                |
|o6 = a*b*x + 3y                 |
|                                |
|o6 : S                          |
+--------------------------------+

Note that in the previous example, linearPart g does not include a but does
include a*b*x

