  * Function: *note randomPointsOnRationalVariety:
    randomPointsOnRationalVariety_lpIdeal_cmZZ_rp,
  * Usage: 
        randomPointsOnRationalVariety(I, n)
        randomPointOnRationalVariety
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, An ideal in a polynomial ring
        $S$ over a field, which defines a prime ideal
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, The number of points to
        generate
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A list of $n$ one row matrices over
        the base field of $S$, that are randomly chosen points on $I$.  null is
        returned in the case when the routine cannot determine if the variety
